Z||000052||coolcat||06-06-2001||03:53 PM||||I've noticed a few of you have made comments about Crystal Method (one of my favorite groups)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> it got me to reminiscing. Well last summer my g/f of the time lived about 40 miles away from my house, so needless to say I made the trip about 3-4 times a week for about two months in my 87GT(man I really miss that car). Well “normally” the trip would take about 55mins,but me being the bonehead that I am .I had it down so that I could do it in about 25-30mins door to door. For all u people saying this kid’s crazy I was doing this at about 1am so there weren’t any cars on the freeway, anyhoo I would always listen to Crystal Method during these trips to get me in the driving mood. Well this one night at about 1:30am I was about half way there and doing about 125mph when all of the sudden the red and blues start flashing in my mirror (scared the livin sh!t outta me) so I start slowing down and starting to pull over . The whole time I’m thinking smart Donovan your gonna loose your license for sure man your sooo screwed. Well I pull over and stop and the cop comes along side of me evil eyeing me as he’s going but then he just takes off no sirens, lights nothing .I nearly passed out.  All I could think of is you lucky idiot he must have been in one he!! of a good mood .Well what I’m getting at is that I don’t listen to Crystal Method while driving late at night any more. BTW that was the only time I saw a cop during my little midnight runs. The next time I got pulled over the officer got out of the car but that’s another story <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Gettin good players is easy,gettin them to play together is the hard part||||reg||1
Z||000053||Raydar||06-06-2001||04:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Butter:<BR><B>Try This:<BR>Hit an open 4 lane and crank up "Born to be Wild"... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually most anything by Steppenwolf will do. I'm kinda partial to "Screaming Night Hog." Makes the woofers talk a bit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000054||FLASHY||06-06-2001||06:36 PM||||OOOOOooooo Man! I forgot about Crystal Method. I LOVE that CD! I forgot I had that....I have to find that CD.....man oh man...This forum paid off again....wooooo hooooo!<P>OK I'm fine now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/flashy_sig.gif"> <P>"I know you believe you understand what you think I wrote, but I'm not sure you realize that what you read is not what I really meant"||||reg||1
Z||000055||Seanh||06-06-2001||07:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>Heavy metal makes my foot heavy!!  Alternative has a habbit of doing it too!<P>Metallica<BR>Korn<BR>Limp Bizkit<BR>White/Rob Zombie<BR>Powerman 5000<BR>Linkin Park<BR>Offspring<BR>AC/DC - Highway To Hell (oh yea)<BR>Guns and Roses<BR>Slipknot<P>Just to name a few   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehehe!<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya know, thats almost got to be my list with the exception of Korn, I don't care much for them. I love Linkin Park's "In the End", its not really a go-fast song, but I still like it. Pretty much anything AC/DC is go-fast musuc. Limp Bizket, I would "My Way" "Rollin"(both, but I like DMX version best), "Livin' it up" "Full Nelson" "My Generation" (love that one). Also one song I noticed today I got the speedo up there while listening to was "Abracadabra" by SugarRay. "Cum on Everybody" by Eminem is a descent speed song, but since I'm sure everyones favorite singer is Eminem....||||reg||1
